{
  "requirement": "The book preprocessor MUST escape requirement names and link targets when inserting badge HTML. It MUST encode badge label and message text in Shields.io URL path components so punctuation cannot change the badge URL structure.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The sources meet `requirements.references.safe_badges`. The tests are a little thin on punctuation, as noted at the end.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `shield_path_component` (src/lib.rs:448, `{impl}`) encodes every byte outside `A-Za-z0-9.` for the Shields.io path.\n  - A space becomes `_`, `_` becomes `__`, and `-` becomes `--`, which are the Shields.io escapes.\n  - Every other byte, including non-ASCII, becomes `%XX`. Characters such as `/`, `?`, `#`, `%` and `&` therefore cannot change the URL structure.\n- `shield_badge` (src/lib.rs:433, `{impl}`) encodes both the label and the message with that function. It then HTML-escapes the full URL for `src` and the label and message for `alt`. The `color` argument comes from fixed constants.\n- `escape_html` (src/lib.rs:774, `{impl}`) escapes `& < > \" '`.\n- `replace_definitions` (`{impl}` at line 302) escapes the full name used in the badge `id`. It also escapes the detail `href` for the badge anchor and the \"See evidence\" link.\n- `replace_references` (`{impl}` at line 409) escapes the `href` for reference badges. The badge image goes through `shield_badge`.\n- The only other badge HTML is `render_detail_sections` in src/index.rs:653. It calls `shield_badge` with fixed state labels and colors, so it is safe through the marked helper and needs no extra marker.\n- The other uses of `escape_html` (commands.rs, fixme.rs, index.rs) sit behind the shared helper. They are not badge-specific behavior added outside the requirement.\n\n**Tests**\n- `shields_badge_urls_escape_requirement_names` (src/lib.rs:998) checks that `_` becomes `__` and `-` becomes `--`, and that spaces become `_`. It also checks that `&` in the query string is rendered as `&amp;`, and that `alt` text is correct.\n- `invalid_names_remain_literal_and_html_is_escaped` (src/lib.rs:983) uses the namespace `a&b` and checks that the rendered `alt` is `req a&amp;b.good`.\n- No test feeds `/`, `?`, `#`, `%` or non-ASCII through the percent-encoding path. No test feeds quotes through the href path. The encoder is a simple, total byte match, so I judge this acceptable.",
